    "long_instructions": "## Do This:\r\n\r\nYou're a QA Engineer at Cartly, an online shopping app. Your manager just messaged you:\r\n\r\n> \"Cart's been acting up. Five bugs reported overnight. Triage and fix in order of severity. Track your work in triage.md.\"\r\n\r\n1. Open `triage.md`. Click each button and observe how the cart changes. For each bug you find, note what happened and rate the severity (high, medium, low).\r\n\r\n2. Based on your notes, decide what order to fix the bugs in.\r\n\r\n3. For each bug, write your best guess: which variable is wrong, and what do you think the bug is? Then share your observation and your guess with AI Tutor and ask for help finding and fixing it.\r\n\r\n4. Fix the code in `script.js` and test again until all five buttons work as expected.",
    "display_name": "Shopping Cart",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/c4401d5b85feedab82eb10ae77d3b4de-shopping.png",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Add products and manage your cart total while shopping online. Debug how actions affect item count, totals, and checkout state.",
